60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A's transport is 38% of costs. Option C is 1,100 yen per night. I need to see which liability is manageable before voting.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B keeps us on campus, but the canteen is closed. That means cooking duty returns. I cannot accept that burden again.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option B keeps us in our own bubbles. Option C is rigid. Option A is the only place where the year-groups are forced to share space.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C’s public beds are quiet, but the lottery is too rigid. Option A offers privacy, but the distance is a risk. I need to weigh rest against logistics.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A’s non-refundable deposit is a liability. Option B has no dropout risk. Option C is rigid. I need to know who absorbs the cost if someone leaves late.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, Option B is a trap. The canteen closure means we repeat last year's labor errors. I cannot endorse a plan that guarantees financial and operational failure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, agreed. Option B is unacceptable. The cooking duty alone would destroy the organizers again. We must avoid that trap.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, I agree. Option B fails on every metric. We need the isolation of Option A to break the silos.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree Option B is out. But Option A’s distance risks the rest I need. I hope the coastal lodge offers genuine quiet for sleep.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, Option A forces interaction, but the non-refundable deposit is a financial trap. I need a strict headcount to prevent individual members from absorbing the loss.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the deposit risk is real, but Option B guarantees the labor and financial gap we just escaped. I need to see if A's transport savings offset that liability.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
